# Copy to apps/api/.env — local development values only. Never commit a real secret.
ENV=development
APP_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string
# Leave unset to use the SQLite dev fallback (ADR-002). PostgreSQL + pgvector:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg2://football:football@localhost:54321/football_os
CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3210,http://127.0.0.1:3210
ACCESS_TOKEN_TTL_MINUTES=15
REFRESH_TOKEN_TTL_DAYS=30
# How long a rotated-out refresh token may still be presented (ADR-003, 2026-09-23). One page load
# fires several proxied calls and each would otherwise spend the same single-use token. Past this
# window a token coming back is treated as a copy and every session for the account is destroyed.
REFRESH_REUSE_GRACE_SECONDS=60

# Provider keys (ADR-005). With none of these set the API runs in DEMO MODE and
# labels every generated payload accordingly — that is a supported state, not an error.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# OpenAI-compatible gateways (e.g. a hosted proxy) can sit in front of the provider: set OPENAI_BASE_URL to its
# /v1 root. The default is https://api.openai.com/v1 and leaves OpenAI proper untouched.
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# Some gateways front their /v1 behind Cloudflare's UA-filtering; if the stock urllib agent earns a 403, set a
# browser UA for just those calls. Unset leaves the default agent alone.
# OPENAI_USER_AGENT=Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/120.0 Safari/537.36
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# NEWS_API_KEY=
# FOOTBALL_DATA_API_KEY=
AI_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=5.00

# Knowledge base (M2). The corpus lives in data/knowledge and is ingested on boot;
# ingestion is idempotent by content hash, so a restart only re-embeds changed files.
# KNOWLEDGE_DIR=/absolute/path/to/data/knowledge
# KNOWLEDGE_AUTO_INGEST=true
# Embeddings: hash-local is deterministic and offline; set to openai with a key above for real vectors.
# Both write the same vector(256) column, so switching providers only needs `python -m seed --force-knowledge`.
# EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=hash-local
# OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL=text-embedding-3-small

# Service plane (Phase 11, Spring Cloud). Absent by default: with EUREKA_URL unset the core
# registers nothing and the app runs exactly as before. The plane is additive — the edge
# discovers the core by name via Eureka; the rate limiter, breaker and trace id apply at the door.
# See docs/runbooks/service_plane.md.
# EUREKA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8761/eureka/
# SERVICE_HOST=127.0.0.1
# SERVICE_NAME=football-core
# SERVICE_PORT=8731

# Redis, if this host has one. The compose profile runs an AUTHENTICATED instance
# (REDIS_PASSWORD, default football — change it); a Redis without a password is refused at the door
# and this API serves from memory with the degraded scope published on every answer
# (X-RateLimit-Scope: process). An authenticated local instance needs its password in the URL:
# REDIS_URL=redis://:football@127.0.0.1:6379/0
# RATE_LIMIT_REDIS_URL=redis://:football@127.0.0.1:6379/1

# Consul / snapshot stores and the trace ledger (M11+). OPS metrics and alerts work without these.
# TACTICS_AUTO_SYNC=true
# TRACE_STORE_ENABLED=true
# OPS_ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL=https://example/webhook
# WORLD_SEED=3
# STORAGE_DIR=./var

# Rate limiting (M15). On in every environment except ENV=test. With no store reachable the limiter
# still runs, per process, and says so on every answer (`X-RateLimit-Scope: process`) — a degraded
# tier is a published state, not a silent one. Point it at Redis to make the budget cluster-wide.
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=1
# The store defaults to REDIS_URL, the cache tier's instance. Set this only to keep the counters
# apart from the evictable cache — they are different workloads and a host may want them separated.
# RATE_LIMIT_REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/1
# REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0
# Only a peer inside one of these networks may name the caller in X-Forwarded-For. The default is
# the loopback pair, where this project's own edge and web tier run. Behind another proxy, add its
# network; behind none, leave it empty — a header anyone can type must not mint a new identity.
# RATE_LIMIT_TRUSTED_PROXIES=127.0.0.1/32,::1/128

# Async jobs (M16). The database row is the truth; the stream is only the wake-up. With no store the
# worker still drains the board by polling, one interval late — so this is a latency knob, not a
# correctness one. A separate logical database keeps the queue out of a cache flush.
# JOB_STREAM_REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/2

# The worker process: `python -m app.worker` (see docs/M16_JOB_STREAM_VERIFICATION.md). The API never
# runs handlers — a request thread that starts a video analysis holds a connection for minutes.
